    "details": "<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Robot Specifications:</strong> The robot must be wireless and meet specific design requirements related to power, pneumatics, hydraulics, and weapon systems.</li>\n<li><strong>Gameplay Regulations:</strong> Matches consist of single rounds (3&ndash;4 minutes), with immediate disqualification for robots that leave the arena or become immobilized.</li>\n<li><strong>Safety Compliance:</strong> Robots must pass safety inspections, with strict guidelines for battery protection, weapon covers, and controlled activation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Format:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Team Composition:</strong> Each team can have a maximum of six participants and must register on the official website.</li>\n<li><strong>Competition Stages:</strong> Teams must submit an abstract (written + video) for selection, followed by group-stage battles leading to knockout rounds.</li>\n<li><strong>Judging Criteria:</strong> Points are awarded based on aggression, control, damage, and strategy, with subjective decisions for tie-breakers</li>\n</ul>",
